abstract: "LAADAN-AC is an offline actor-critic framework that embeds benchmark-defined action admissibility directly in policy optimisation. The release contains fixed epoch-1000 experiments on ICU-Sepsis, an exploratory eICU-CRD Demo MDP evaluation, component ablations, paired post-hoc masking diagnostics, checkpoints, and provenance."
keywords:
  - offline reinforcement learning
  - sepsis treatment
  - admissible action masking
  - constrained policy learning
  - healthcare artificial intelligence
